# Sample Lockfile

File: opm/examples/lock.oot

A lockfile pins the exact set of installed packages. It is regenerated on every successful install. Path: `.ooda_modules/lock`.

There is one format. Header lines, then package lines:

```
v2
oodac#<sha>
std#<sha>
hello-world@1.2.3#9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08#unpinned#FsRead
json-parser@2.1.0#e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855#unpinned#FsRead
http-client@1.5.4#5d41402abc4b2a76b9719d911017c592a2b5a8e0c6b7c4e8a3c2d3a4b5c6d7e8#unpinned#FsWrite
```

## Format

Header:

- `v2`
- `oodac#<sha>` — hash of the compiler pin
- `std#<sha>` — hash of `std.pin`

Each package line is `name@version#sha256#commit#CapName`.
`lock/lock.oo` sorts and hashes those lines. `lock/v2.oo` is replace, override, and local git pin on the same file. Not a second format.

A mismatch against live CAS bytes is a hard fail.
